1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Rome's harbour walls have taken two thousand years of salt and storm, and many are still standing.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Modern concrete poured for the same job can crack apart in fifty.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:17,500
The Roman recipe was volcanic ash, quicklime, and seawater.

4
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:24,500
That mixture slowly grew rare crystals, aluminous tobermorite, that knitted the mortar together.

5
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:30,500
The salt that rusts modern steel was actually feeding the Roman chemistry.

6
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:37,500
Engineers now study those ancient recipes to design concrete that lasts.
